Here are two ways to polish the text, depending on your preferred style (a formal patent specification style or a clear, modern technical description). Both options preserve all original reference numbers, steps, and technical details.

### Option 1: Formal Patent & Legal Style (Recommended)
> A printed circuit board (1) comprises an insulating layer (2) and a conductive layer (3) disposed on the insulating layer (2), structured to form a contact surface (4) for an electronic component (11) to be mounted on the printed circuit board (1). Within the region of the contact surface (4), at least one channel (8) extends through both the contact surface (4) and the insulating layer (2) and is filled with a thermally conductive material. 
> 
> The process is characterized by the steps of:
> * Preparing an insulating layer (2) joined with a conductive layer (3);
> * Forming at least one channel (8) extending through the conductive layer (2) and the insulating layer (3);
> * Lining the channel (8) with a thermally conductive material;
> * Structuring the conductive layer (3) into a contact surface (4) for receiving the electronic component (11);
> * Applying a solder deposit (9) that at least minimally overlaps with the contact surface (4);
> * Positioning the electronic component (11); and
> * Melting the solder and allowing the assembly to cool.

---

### Option 2: Modern Technical Documentation Style (Fluid & Direct)
> A printed circuit board (1) includes an insulating layer (2) and an adjoining conductive layer (3), which is structured into a contact surface (4) for an electronic component (11). In the region of the contact surface (4), at least one channel (8) filled with a thermally conductive material passes through both the contact surface (4) and the insulating layer (2). 
> 
> The manufacturing process comprises the following steps:
> 1. Preparing an insulating layer (2) connected to a conductive layer (3);
> 2. Creating at least one channel (8) through the conductive layer (2) and the insulating layer (3);
> 3. Lining the channel (8) with a thermally conductive material;
> 4. Structuring the conductive layer (3) into a contact surface (4) for the component (11);
> 5. Depositing solder (9) such that it at least minimally overlaps the contact surface (4);
> 6. Placing the electronic component (11); and
> 7. Melting the solder and cooling the assembly.

### Key Improvements Made:
* **Syntax & Flow:** Broken down the initial run-on sentence into clearer, more structured clauses.
* **Professional Terminology:** Replaced informal phrases like *"setting down"* with precise technical terms such as *"positioning"* or *"placing"*.
* **Readability:** Changed *"populating an electronic component"* to *"mounting/receiving an electronic component"* and formatted the process steps into a clean bulleted/numbered list for better visual structure.
